WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.169
-Welcome.
Thank you so much, everybody.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.604
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:09.709
We are coming to you live
right now from Studio 6A.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.213
After the final debate between
President Trump and Joe Biden,

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:16.549
and I think we can all agree
the winner was Kristen Welker.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.218
I mean, come on.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.086
Knockout.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.420
Home run.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.523
Of course, everyone was
talking about how there would be

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.992
a mute button used during
tonight's debate.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.293
It seemed like it
worked pretty well.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.262
I'm thinking of getting one
for Thanksgiving.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:32.365
The muted mics
really helped, though.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.600
It thought it was much calmer.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.967
At one point, they almost cut to

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:40.773
Jeffrey Toobin
to liven things up.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.809
Yeah, Trump seemed
much more calm.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.210
People were like,
"Did they replace him

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.013
with his Disney robot?"

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.814
For the most part,
things were pretty civil

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:50.683
compared to the first debate,
which was basically

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.852
a UFC fight on meth.

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:55.187
Yeah, it was a lot nicer.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.356
If the first debate was
sponsored by Red Bull,

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:00.526
this one
was sponsored by NyQuil.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:03.129
Everyone was impressed by Trump
not interrupting or yelling.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.764
I'm not sure it's a great sign
that we talk about the president

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:08.901
like we talk about a 4-year-old
at a puppet show, but...

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:13.038
"You did a great job.
You really did."

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.674
That's right -- tonight,
we saw an all-new Trump.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:21.014
Instead of shouting baseless
accusations, he whispered them.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.781
Trump held in
his anger for so long,

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:23.916
as soon as the debate was over,

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.818
he chewed off the armrest
in his limo.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:30.156
[ Growling ]

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.224
Yeah, no one seemed to get
too riled up.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:35.395
The only person who was really
upset was Chris Wallace.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.930
"Oh, that's how you do it."

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.431
And this was fun.

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:42.168
A lot of people played drinking
games during tonight's debate.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.337
If you did a shot every time
Biden said "Come on,"

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:49.007
you were unconscious by 9:15.

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:52.011
[ Mumbling ] Come on!

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.512
But tonight's debate
was considered a win

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.015
for the Trump campaign,
mostly because he didn't walk in

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.585
with a highly
contagious disease.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.988
Actually, they were supposed to
have two Plexiglas barriers

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.356
separating Trump and Biden,
but they ultimately

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:05.858
decided against it.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:09.095
So make that two more walls
Trump couldn't build.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.129
-Ooh!

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:13.166
-Ooh! Ooh!
That's the "ooh"?

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.936
I got the "ooh" for that one?
-Ooh-ooh!

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.472
-Ooh-ooh!

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.574
Before the debate --
-Ooh!

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.576
-Ooh! Oh!

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.877
That's my jam.
That's what I do.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:27.413
I come out,
and everyone goes, "Ooh!

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.082
Jimmy, don't hurt 'em."

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.284
Before the debate,
it was announced

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.887
that Joe Biden tested
negative for coronavirus.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.888
Meanwhile, Trump
is on so many steroids,

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.825
he tested positive for
Lance Armstrong.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:46.265
Heading into tonight, anywhere
between 2% and 8% of Americans

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.133
were still undecided.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:50.603
I just want to say if, after
tonight, you're still undecided,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.439
then, well, we couldn't pick
a joke for this one,

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:57.910
but we'll figure it out
in a week.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.914
Tonight's debate had six
topics -- fighting COVID-19,

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.215
national security,
American families,

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:06.485
race in America, climate change,
and whether Rudy Giuliani

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:08.955
was actually tucking in
his shirt.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.761
But after a slow start,
Trump made a lot of accusations

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:17.730
about Biden and his family,
so Joe tried to turn

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.499
the conversation to the families
watching at home.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:24.137 line:0%
-There's a very strong e-mail
talking about

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.906 line:0%
your family wanting to make
$10 million a year.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.876 line:0%
-He doesn't want to talk about
the substantive issues.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.877 line:0%
It's not about
his family and my family.

00:03:31.877 --> 00:03:33.112 line:0%
It about your family.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.248 line:0%
But that's the last thing
he wants to talk about.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.149
Trump was like, "Trust me --

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:40.553
in our household, it's never
been about my family."

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.456
After Trump accused Biden
of wanting to destroy

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:46.859
Social Security and Medicare,
Biden pointed out that

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.128
Trump might have the wrong guy.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.329 line:0%
-Very confused guy.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.997 line:0%
He thinks he's running
against somebody else.

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:54.233 line:0%
He's running against Joe Biden.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.768 line:0%
I beat all those other people

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.603 line:0%
because I disagreed with them.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.372 line:0%
Joe Biden he's running against.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:03.775
-Whoa! Biden was fired up.
Trump was like, "Wow.

00:04:03.775 --> 00:04:07.613
Give me whatever
steroids he's on."

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.882
Later, Kristen Welker asked
if Trump's language

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.651
was contributing to a climate
of hate in our country.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.019
Check out what he had to say.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.456 line:0%
-I am the least-racist person
in this room.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.626 line:0%
I can't even see the audience
because it's so dark,

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.928 line:0%
but I don't care
who's in the audience.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:25.231 line:0%
I'm the least-racist person
in this room.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:28.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:29.836
-Then, instead of
the mute button,

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.472
someone hit the laugh track.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.605
It's a little weird to say,

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:35.274
"I'm the least-racist person
in the room"

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.309
when half the room
are your friends and family.

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:42.481
It's like,
"He's more racist than I am."

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:45.151
But since this was
the last debate,

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.119
both candidates wanted to make
their closing arguments

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:48.453
to the American people.

00:04:48.453 --> 00:04:51.357
Let take a look at one of
Trump's closing arguments now.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.394
♪♪

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:56.461 line:0%
-I know more about wind
than you do.

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:58.564 line:0%
It's extremely expensive.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.132 line:0%
It kills all the birds.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:03.269
♪♪

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:08.007
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.676
-What?

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.977
Actually, that's not all.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.280
Trump has been making
closing arguments all week.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.381
Here's another one.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.418
♪♪

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:22.121 line:0%
-This was caused by Russia.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.422 line:0%
Russia.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:26.559
♪♪

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.328
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.930
-He's really trying to get
the word out.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.533
Let's see another
closing argument from Trump.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.570
♪♪

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.540 line:0%
-COVID, COVID, COVID, COVID,
COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.542 line:0%
[ Crowd boos ]
COVID, COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.679
♪♪

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:50.883
-Do we have any more
closing arguments from Trump?

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.919
♪♪
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:58.224 line:0%
-And with us, as well,
are members of the incredible

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:05.464 line:0%
Lumbee...Keetoowah...tribes.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.133 line:0%
Lumbee Keetoowah.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.269
♪♪

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:13.605
-Oh, come on. Okay.

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.841
Alright, just one more.
One more.

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:18.878
♪♪

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.613 line:0%
-"What kind of ice cream
are you eating?"

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:23.482 line:0%
"Uh, chocolate."

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:26.619
♪♪

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.755
-Oh, my goodness.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:32.024
Unbelievable.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:34.226
Well, Trump had a busy day.

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.528
After walking out of yesterday's
interview with "60 Minutes,"

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.797
today, he decided to post
the footage early.

00:06:38.797 --> 00:06:40.466
I guess he thought it would
help him look better,

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:41.734
but I'm not really sure why.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:42.969
Watch this.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.672 line:0%
-No, I'm not.

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:47.840 line:0%
Well, I'm gonna be fair.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.976 line:0%
You don't ask Biden
tough questions.

00:06:50.976 --> 00:06:54.680 line:0%
Huh? It's terrible.
It's terrible.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.516 line:0%
"Are you ready
for tough questions?"

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:59.652 line:0%
That's no way to talk.

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:04.223 line:0%
I think we have enough of
an interview here.

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:06.259 line:0%
Okay? That's enough.
Let's go.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.461
-He's the most powerful man
in the world,

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.463
and he spends his time making
bootleg episodes

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:13.098
of "60 Minutes."

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:15.434
Trump tried to embarrass
Lesley Stahl by leaking a video

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.102
of her asking tough questions.

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:19.138
Isn't that her job?

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.472
Next, he's gonna embarrass
Bobby Flay

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:23.108
by leaking videos of him
making paella.

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:26.345
[ As Trump ]
You just got served, Bobby.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:27.646
[ Normal voice ]
Also, did you see him

00:07:27.646 --> 00:07:30.416
drink the water with two hands?

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:32.685
I'm just glad he's back
to full strength.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.154
Aren't you happy?

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.990
How...
[ Applause ]

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.794
How is he still drinking water
with two hands?

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.395
He's like, "Joe Biden is weak.

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:44.997
[ Slurps ]

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:48.133
He doesn't have the physical
stamina to be president.

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:49.969
[ Slurps ]

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.805
Very, very poor health,
Joe Biden."

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.741
But this is interesting.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.075
Before tonight's debate,
they announced

00:07:57.075 --> 00:07:59.512
a record-breaking number
of people have already voted --

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:01.180
nearly 48 million.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.615
I guess that explains...

00:08:02.615 --> 00:08:05.818
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:07.286
I guess that explains why,
three hours ago,

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:10.990
48 million people
tuned into Netflix.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.025
Asked when they made up
their mind,

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:16.829
early voters were like,
"March 2020."

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.330
You know Trump
is thinking, "Wow.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:21.601
48 million people
couldn't wait to re-elect me."

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:26.105
It makes sense that so many
people were able to do it.

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.439
Voting is the only
plan we've had

00:08:27.439 --> 00:08:30.442
on our calendars
in seven months.

00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:32.144
This actually
could be something.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:34.279
Apparently, NASA
has a big announcement.

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:35.448
Listen to this.

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:37.816 line:0%
-Apparently, NASA's made
an exciting new discovery

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:38.985 line:0%
about the moon.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:42.087 line:0%
There is a huge announcement
coming from NASA,

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.755 line:0%
but we have to wait
until Monday.

00:08:43.755 --> 00:08:48.694
-NASA, you know I love you,
but come on.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.095
We're living through a pandemic.

00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:55.401
The last thing we need right now
is a cliffhanger about the moon.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.802
Just tell us.

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:59.171
That's like Dr. Fauci saying,
"I have some exciting news

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.006
about the virus
that I'll tell you...

00:09:01.006 --> 00:09:04.076
right after the break."

00:09:04.076 --> 00:09:06.044
It's 2020, so part of me
is definitely worried

00:09:06.044 --> 00:09:07.580
that we're about
to find out that the moon

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.249
once partied with
Jeffrey Epstein.

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:16.255
Americans were like,
"Unless it's gonna 'splode,

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:19.925
we do not a-care."

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:21.393
Some sports news.

00:09:21.393 --> 00:09:24.296
The NFL just announced that if
games keep getting pushed back

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:25.597
because of COVID,
it could affect

00:09:25.597 --> 00:09:27.699
when the season actually ends.

00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:29.601 line:0%
-The NFL acknowledged yesterday
the Super Bowl

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:33.805 line:0%
could be moved to March if games
keep having to be postponed.

00:09:33.805 --> 00:09:35.908
-Yeah, the NFL
told all the players

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:38.143
to keep their schedules open,
except the Jets.

00:09:38.143 --> 00:09:42.081
They can start making
other plans.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:43.382
That's right --
the NFL said the decision

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:45.784
will be made by league
officials, medical experts,

00:09:45.784 --> 00:09:47.486
and Patrick Mahomes.

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.688
"Yeah, I suppose that time
works for me. Yeah."

00:09:49.688 --> 00:09:51.156
Honestly, I don't care.

00:09:51.156 --> 00:09:54.694
I lost interest in the NFL once
they cancelled the Pro Bowl.

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:01.633
I mean, why even have a season,
right, guys?

00:10:01.633 --> 00:10:04.436
And, finally, a bank in
California had a break-in,

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:06.472
but the thieves
aren't exactly who you'd expect.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:07.873
Watch this.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:11.043 line:0%
-Two masked bandits broke into
a California bank Tuesday,

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.945 line:0%
but they didn't get away
with any cash.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.546 line:0%
Check out the culprits.

00:10:14.546 --> 00:10:18.083 line:0%
Yeah, they're not bank robbers,
but a couple of raccoons.

00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:20.386
-Yeah. Police were like, "Aww,"

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:24.289
until they realized one raccoon
was wanted for triple homicide.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:25.824
Meanwhile,
another raccoon was outside

00:10:25.824 --> 00:10:27.626
hacking into
the security system.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:32.999
"I just need three more seconds,
and -- Yeah, we're in."

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.534
Yep, they're the only ones to
ever break into a bank like,

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.470
"Just give us all the trash,
and no one gets hurt"

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.973
We have a great show tonight.

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:43.174
Thank you for watching.
We're live here.

00:10:43.174 --> 00:10:44.443
Give it up for The Roots.

